WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:06.700
Speaker 1: So when Joe Biden won in November,
we started a conversation about what will

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:08.670
Joe Biden be able to get done?

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:13.269
What will be the parameters and the limits
of what Joe Biden can do.

00:00:13.269 --> 00:00:17.529
And I made the case that Joe Manchin, the
Democratic senator from West Virginia, who

00:00:17.529 --> 00:00:22.840
is arguably the most right wing of the Democratic
senators, was really going to be a problem,

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:28.029
was really going to be an impediment, was
really going to be a major obstacle.

00:00:28.029 --> 00:00:30.340
And some people in the audience got it.

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:37.610
But many wrote to me and said, David, you
know, I think you're overstating the case

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:39.840
about Joe Manchin here.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:40.900
And I maintained, no, I'm not.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:49.500
No, I believe that Joe Manchin really is going
to be this big of a problem.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:53.450
And we are now learning just how big of a
problem Joe Manchin is going to be.

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:56.970
CNN reports Democratic Senator Joe Manchin
on Sunday yesterday defended his decision

00:00:56.970 --> 00:01:04.890
to vote against a sweeping voting rights bill
and reiterated his opposition to gutting the

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:09.400
filibuster, declaring in the strongest terms
yet that he is not willing to change Senate

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:12.930
rules to help his party push through much
of Joe Biden's agenda.

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:17.040
Manchin said they call him a moderate Democrat,
which is a very favorable term.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:21.110
Manchin said, quote, I believe that partizan
voting legislation will destroy the already

00:01:21.110 --> 00:01:24.600
weakening binds of our democracy.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:28.950
And for that reason, I will vote against the
for the people act further.

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:32.180
I will not vote to weaken or eliminate the
filibuster.

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:34.090
This is what's so sick about this position.

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:35.759
It's basically a both sides type position.

00:01:35.759 --> 00:01:41.080
What I mean by that is Joe Manchin is saying,
well, if I am going to do voting rights legislation,

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:43.350
I don't want it to be partizan or one sided.

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:46.750
But the problem is that the other side, the
Republican Party, is using disenfranchisement

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:48.360
as a tool to try to win elections.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:52.830
Joe Manchin seems to think and maybe he believes
it or maybe he's just saying it, that if one

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:55.890
side wants to pass partizan legislation to
prevent people from being able to legally

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:59.500
vote and the other side wants to pass legislation
to ensure everyone who's entitled to vote

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:02.130
can vote, they're both simply partizan voting
rights, pieces of legislation.

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:05.320
This is it's hard to imagine a more depraved
sort of both sides type argument.

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:08.890
And this is exactly what I feared would happen
with Joe Manchin.

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:11.090
And it is indeed happening.

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:17.390
Huffington Post is also reporting about this,
saying that Senator Joe Manchin said he won't

00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:19.760
vote for his party's for the People Act, a
bill focused on expanding voting rights.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:20.760
Again, the idea that.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:24.100
Limiting voting rights, which is against the
Constitution, against the law, against what

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:27.730
this country is built on and expanding voting
rights for people who can legally vote are

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:28.940
just two sides of the same political coin.

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:32.520
That is the full end position toxicity level
of the idea of the enlightened centrist.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:36.010
And I'm not going to be super partizan on
either side.

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:39.630
When one side is trying to take rights away.

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:43.880
You can't say, well, I don't want to get involved
on this side either, because we're just as

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:45.650
partizan and trying to make sure people have
their rights.

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:47.790
That's not the way it works.

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:57.500
And this is the sort of you know, I use the
term enlightened centrism sometimes to refer

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:02.260
to online commentators or whatever who want
to pretend to kind of be above the partizan

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:03.260
fray and see both sides.

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:07.090
But this is one of 100 members of the U.S.
Senate who is equating taking voting rights

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:13.950
away as a partizan act by Republicans to giving
voting rights as a partizan act by Democrats

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:25.520
when the reality is what the Constitution
says and what the law says should be the guiding

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:26.520
principle here.

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:29.959
So it's truly unbelievable and disgusting.

00:03:29.959 --> 00:03:41.190
Kirsten Sinema on the Democratic side, also
arguably a problem in some areas and will

00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:55.840
ultimately see what happens with this for
for the people act.

00:03:55.840 --> 00:04:00.959
But this does not look good.

00:04:00.959 --> 00:04:07.480
Now, I know that many people will say, well,
David, then let's primary Joe Manchin.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:10.489
I'm not against primary anybody, as I've said
before, primary, whoever the hell you want,

00:04:10.489 --> 00:04:12.269
simply understand what the consequences of
that might be.

00:04:12.269 --> 00:04:14.870
I don't see how a more progressive Democrat
wins in West Virginia.

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:26.620
My instinct is based on the Pew polling data
I've seen out of West Virginia, that if you

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:33.689
successfully primary Joe Manchin with a more
progressive Democrat, which I don't even know

00:04:33.689 --> 00:04:38.650
if one would win, but if Joe Manchin loses
a Democratic primary to a more progressive

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:42.660
Democrat, it seems almost certain that more
progressive Democrat loses the eventual general

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:43.660
election.

00:04:43.660 --> 00:05:00.219
And then you have a Republican in that seat.

00:05:00.219 --> 00:05:02.199
So obviously, this is disgusting.

00:05:02.199 --> 00:05:05.479
Obviously, I find all of this completely disgusting
and counterproductive and retrograde.

00:05:05.479 --> 00:05:09.439
And it's exactly what we predicted in November
was going to happen.

00:05:09.439 --> 00:05:11.349
So I'm not surprised by it.

00:05:11.349 --> 00:05:14.779
But Manchin still mostly votes for Democrats.

00:05:14.779 --> 00:05:16.960
So I'm not defending the guy.

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:19.880
I'm merely saying you're playing with fire.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:30.909
If what you might do to fix the Joe Manchin
problem loses Democrats, the majority in the

00:05:30.909 --> 00:05:31.909
Senate.

00:05:31.909 --> 00:05:37.590
Now, of course, there will be other races
as well when Joe Manchin is up.

00:05:37.590 --> 00:05:39.949
So it's more complicated than that.

00:05:39.949 --> 00:05:49.460
But I'm curious to hear from you about it,
because it's not at all clear to me that the

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:59.379
wind the way to win this is by removing Manchin
and putting at risk that seat maybe being

00:05:59.379 --> 00:06:00.740
taken over by a Republican.

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:04.550
I would be you know, my instinct is Biden
talks about how great a negotiator he is.

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:07.240
Well, negotiate with this guy.

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:11.900
Biden brags about negotiating across the aisle,
negotiate with your own side to get this guy

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:25.949
on board if you're really the great diplomat
and negotiator you claim to be.

00:06:25.949 --> 00:06:28.629
And in some senses, Joe Biden is a good negotiator.

00:06:28.629 --> 00:06:32.659
He's done some some good things negotiating,
then convince this guy.

00:06:32.659 --> 00:06:34.499
What are we waiting for?

00:06:34.499 --> 00:06:41.639
I think we need to find a way to push mankind
into supporting at least some of this stuff

00:06:41.639 --> 00:06:50.289
because the risk of losing him to a Republican
in that seat to me seems great.

00:06:50.289 --> 00:06:54.499
I'm curious if the risk is great.

00:06:54.499 --> 00:07:05.020
It's not a good thing to be clear.

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:08.309
Let me know what you think.

00:07:08.309 --> 00:07:25.930
I want to hear from 
you about it

